      "message": "feat(turning): threading infeed method and decreasing-depth pass schedule\n\nA Threading op now carries an infeed plan: radial, flank (with a\ncompound angle) or alternating-flank infeed; constant-depth or\nconstant-area (first depth x sqrt(n), clamped at a minimum depth per\npass) schedule; a finish allowance; and spring passes at full depth.\nThe kernel lays the pass list from it (turning::infeed), shifting\neach flank pass's start along the lattice by its height above the\nroot x tan(angle) - same lead, same spindle phase - and the verdict\njudges the laid V. A flank angle past the insert's half-angle, a\nminimum depth past the first depth, an allowance as deep as the\nthread, or too many spring passes are refused by name at Create /\nPaste / Edit / retype (thread_gate) and again at Generate.\n\nThe default plan reproduces the old ladder exactly: no golden moved,\nthe stamp digests the plan only when it is not the default, and the\nproject key is written only when it is not the default (no version\nstep). The thread-cycle record takes the plan's allowance, spring\npasses and flank angle (included, 2x); alternating infeed carries no\nrecord. UI: the Passes tab gains the plan's rows.\n\nFixes #416\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
